@essay rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · LYRIS · THE MACHINERY AROUND HER"
# The machinery around her
drop: Lyris lives inside the most watched marriage in the Empire. The powerful have their intimacy taken from them on purpose, because citizens invested in Imperial marriages won't overthrow the family whose love story they followed (CR).
She answers the watching with the Arrangement, a network of about forty wives that's never once let a widow fall below Stewardwife (CR). She answers her son's death with a secret that only four people hold (TL). And she answers the Trials by watching them with "specific and personal interest" (TL), because the woman Judah marries will become either her successor in the network or its first real threat.
side:
chips: CR, TL, TR
k: The Widowed Covenant
stext: Two years of protection for an Anointed widow, then remarriage or Stewardwife. Her network has made sure no one has ever dropped (CR).
marg
see: Vol. I, the Arrangement, {v1:arrangement}.
/end

@page rh="THE HOUSE OF VANE · LYRIS · EXCAVATION · ELEVEN MINUTES" m="TKC: TR · CR; WRITING"
# Eleven minutes
The Anointed Evening, four hours in the Crown Palace reception hall, cameras in the hall and not the side rooms. Eden spends eleven minutes with Lyris. Lyris says three things that aren't on any Broadcast record, and the third is a warning that's also, if you know how to hear it, a set of instructions. Judah watches from across the hall. He's never seen his mother spend eleven uninterrupted minutes with a candidate (TR).
prompt: 1 · The first thing | 4
prompt: 2 · The second thing | 4
prompt: 3 · The third thing, the warning and the instructions | fill

